---
import LegalPageLayout from '../components/legal/LegalPageLayout.astro';
import { siteSettings } from '../lib/sanity/data';
---

<LegalPageLayout
  title="Modern Slavery Statement"
  eyebrow="SUPPLY CHAIN DUE DILIGENCE & ETHICS"
  subheading="Modern Slavery Act 2015 Section 54 compliance statement detailing Techsteps UK Limited's zero-tolerance approach to modern slavery, forced labour, and human trafficking."
  metaTitle="Modern Slavery Statement | Section 54 Compliance | Techsteps UK"
  metaDescription="Techsteps UK Modern Slavery Statement. Read our formal commitments under the UK Modern Slavery Act 2015, supplier audit procedures, employee vetting, and reporting."
  complianceBadge="Modern Slavery Act 2015 Compliant"
  activeSlug="modern-slavery-statement"
  lastUpdated="February 2026"
>
  <section class="space-y-4">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 font-display tracking-tight border-b border-slate-200 pb-3">
      1. Organizational Stance &amp; Policy Scope
    </h2>
    <p>
      This statement is published pursuant to Section 54(1) of the Modern Slavery Act 2015 and constitutes the modern slavery and human trafficking statement of {siteSettings.legalName} ("Techsteps") for the financial year ending 2025/2026.
    </p>
    <p>
      Techsteps maintains a definitive zero-tolerance policy towards all forms of modern slavery, servitude, forced or compulsory labour, and human trafficking across our direct workforce, subcontracted logistics, and global material supply chains. We are firmly committed to acting ethically, transparently, and with integrity in all commercial transactions.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-4">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 font-display tracking-tight border-b border-slate-200 pb-3">
      2. Business Structure &amp; Supply Chain Overview
    </h2>
    <p>
      Techsteps operates nationwide across the United Kingdom, delivering mission-critical Information Management, IT Lifecycle Services &amp; Disposition (ITAD), Secure Destruction, and Commercial Relocations.
    </p>
    <p>
      Our supply chain encompasses:
    </p>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5 text-slate-600">
      <li><strong>Transport &amp; Fleet Partners:</strong> UK commercial vehicle manufacturers, specialized security equipment suppliers, and telemetry providers.</li>
      <li><strong>Hardware Processing &amp; Recycling Partners:</strong> Environment Agency licensed secondary raw material refiners, accredited precious metal smelters, and authorized WEEE treatment facilities (AATFs).</li>
      <li><strong>Facilities &amp; Security Services:</strong> Physical security infrastructure providers, access control system integrators, and independent UK compliance auditors.</li>
      <li><strong>Direct Operational Staff:</strong> Employed drivers, logistics operatives, archival vault technicians, and data destruction engineers.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-4">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 font-display tracking-tight border-b border-slate-200 pb-3">
      3. Strict Recruitment &amp; Employee Vetting Standards
    </h2>
    <p>
      Because our operatives handle confidential data-bearing hardware and government archives, we enforce the most rigorous employment screening in the UK industry:
    </p>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
      <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200/90">
        <h4 class="font-bold text-slate-900 text-sm">Mandatory BS 7858 Screening</h4>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 mt-1">100% of employees undergo comprehensive 5-year employment verification, financial probity checks, and enhanced criminal record checks prior to commencing work.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200/90">
        <h4 class="font-bold text-slate-900 text-sm">Real Living Wage Employer</h4>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 mt-1">We are committed to paying all employees at or above the independently calculated Real Living Wage, mitigating the financial vulnerability that can lead to worker exploitation.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200/90">
        <h4 class="font-bold text-slate-900 text-sm">Direct Employment Priority</h4>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 mt-1">We prioritize direct permanent employment contracts over agency temporary labour, ensuring transparent working conditions and statutory employment rights.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200/90">
        <h4 class="font-bold text-slate-900 text-sm">Right to Work Verification</h4>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 mt-1">Robust physical and Home Office digital share-code right-to-work verification is conducted for every candidate without exception.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-4">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 font-display tracking-tight border-b border-slate-200 pb-3">
      4. Downstream Supplier Due Diligence &amp; Audits
    </h2>
    <p>
      Given that the global electronics and precious metal refining sector can present inherent supply chain risks, Techsteps mitigates exposure through strict due diligence:
    </p>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-slate-600">
      <li>
        <strong>Tier-1 Smelter Audits:</strong> We only partner with secondary refiners that demonstrate documented chain of custody and certified compliance with European and UK environmental and ethical standards.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Contractual Anti-Slavery Covenants:</strong> All supplier master service agreements include binding clauses requiring adherence to the Modern Slavery Act 2015, with right-to-audit and immediate contract termination remedies for non-compliance.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Prohibition on Unverified Subcontracting:</strong> Downstream material partners are contractually barred from subcontracting material fractions to unvetted third parties without prior written consent from Techsteps.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-4">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 font-display tracking-tight border-b border-slate-200 pb-3">
      5. Whistleblowing &amp; Anonymous Reporting
    </h2>
    <p>
      Techsteps actively encourages all employees, agency contractors, and supply chain partners to report any suspicion of modern slavery, human exploitation, or unfair labor practices without fear of retaliation.
    </p>
    <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200 space-y-1.5 text-xs sm:text-sm font-mono">
      <div><strong>Confidential Whistleblowing Line:</strong> <a href="mailto:whistleblowing@techsteps.co.uk" class="text-emerald-700 hover:underline">whistleblowing@techsteps.co.uk</a></div>
      <div><strong>Compliance Director:</strong> Direct confidential phone line available via {siteSettings.phone}</div>
      <div><strong>UK Modern Slavery Helpline:</strong> 08000 121 700 (<a href="https://www.modernslaveryhelpline.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-emerald-700 underline">modernslaveryhelpline.org</a>)</div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="space-y-4">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 font-display tracking-tight border-b border-slate-200 pb-3">
      6. Board Approval &amp; Executive Sign-Off
    </h2>
    <p>
      This statement has been formally reviewed and approved by the Board of Directors of {siteSettings.legalName} and will be updated annually in accordance with UK statutory reporting requirements.
    </p>
    <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-slate-100 border border-slate-200 text-xs sm:text-sm font-mono space-y-1">
      <div><strong>Approved by:</strong> Board of Directors, {siteSettings.legalName}</div>
      <div><strong>Date of Board Sign-off:</strong> 1st February 2026</div>
      <div><strong>Registered Office:</strong> {siteSettings.address.street}, {siteSettings.address.city}, {siteSettings.address.postcode}</div>
    </div>
  </section>
</LegalPageLayout>
